## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/curve3d.html
- Summary (EN): Lets you hand-draw cubic Bezier curves in the viewport, like 2D illustration software, and also creates polylines and NURBS curves. Used for tracing images, drawing logos and making profile curves for extrusions or revolves.
- Résumé (FR) : Dessine à la main des courbes de Bezier cubiques dans la vue, ainsi que des polylignes et des NURBS, pour tracer contours et profils.

- Inputs meaning: ["none listed on the page; the only documented output is curves", "curve nodes can be chained, with group parameters picking up point groups from previous nodes"]

- Key parameters: ["Primitive Type: Polygon, NURBS Curve or Bezier Curve", "Order: curve order, default 4 (cubic)", "Mode: Select/Edit, Draw, Auto-Bezier Draw or Orient", "Reinterpret Curves as Current Type and Order: converts existing curves when on", "Corner, Smooth and Auto Points Group: group names storing each point type", "Name: name attribute on created geometry, default $OS", "Orient, X/Y/Z Axis: attribute names for orientations", "View Rounded Corners and Round Corner Radius", "Soft Transform Radius: falloff radius for soft transforms", "Approximate Shape on Delete and Approximate End Tangents"]

- Caveats: ["In shaded mode closed Bezier curves may not fill; use wireframe (W).", "Arcs are not perfectly round because weighted Bezier curves are not created.", "In a perspective view drawing snaps to the view-facing or construction plane; an orthographic view is easier for flat shapes.", "Esc switches to the View tool; reselect the node and press Enter to return to the Handles tool."]

